<li about="#cite_note-Astronomy-205" id="cite_note-Astronomy-205" data-mw-footnote-number="203"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFy8"><a href="#cite_ref-Astronomy_205-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFzA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFzE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Astronomy-205" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt748" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwFzI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFRunyonStern2018" class="citation web cs1">Runyon, Kirby D.; Stern, S. Alan (17 May 2018). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.astronomy.com/magazine/2018/05/an-organically-grown-planet-definition" class="external text" id="mwFzM">"An organically grown planet definition — Should we really define a word by voting?"</a>. <i id="mwFzQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronomy_(magazine)" title="Astronomy (magazine)" id="mwFzU">Astronomy</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20191010153028/http://astronomy.com/magazine/2018/05/an-organically-grown-planet-definition" class="external text" id="mwFzY">Archived</a> from the original on 10 October 2019<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwFzc">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwFzg">12 October</span> 2019</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Astronomy&amp;rft.atitle=An+organically+grown+planet+definition+%E2%80%94+Should+we+really+define+a+word+by+voting%3F&amp;rft.date=2018-05-17&amp;rft.aulast=Runyon&amp;rft.aufirst=Kirby+D.&amp;rft.au=Stern%2C+S.+Alan&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.astronomy.com%2Fmagazine%2F2018%2F05%2Fan-organically-grown-planet-definition&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3APlanet" class="Z3988" id="mwFzk"></span></span></li>
